From 55dcec0c2f353ae5211d123587ea229f75253a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:07:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 48/59] ntdll: Route Direct3D modules to the Mullion (DXMT)
 runtime per process.

From WineForge (graphics_policy, launcher_policy, dxmt_loader), adapted for arm64 hosts:
- GRAPHICS_BACKEND/ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=dxmt routes dxgi, d3d10core, d3d11, d3d12,
  d3d12core and winemetal to DXMT_RUNTIME_DIR, which defaults to the bundled lib/mullion.
- The runtime is ARM64X (aarch64-windows) for native ARM64 and x86_64 (ARM64EC) processes,
  i386-windows for WoW64; winemetal.so comes from aarch64-unix and is loaded immediately.
- D3DMetal is x86_64-only and is mapped to Wine's own backend with a warning.
- Launcher policies (Battle.net/Ubisoft to DXMT, software CEF detection) and the
  Battle.net CEF renderer write-copy protection quirk come along.
